<title>USA: Chiron senior vp-finance resigns.</title>
<headline>Chiron senior vp-finance resigns.</headline>
<dateline>EMERYVILLE, Calif. 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chiron Corp said Dennis Winger resigned as senior vice president of finance and administration, effective August 31, in order to take a new assignment in a major company.</p>
<p>Winger joined Chiron in 1989 as chief financial officer.</p>
<p>Edward Penhoet, Chiron president, will oversee Winger's responsibilities until a replacement is named, Chiron said.</p>
<p>Chiron is a healthcare company that combines diagnostic, vaccine and therapeutic strategies for controlling disease.</p>
